<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  One file, three bundles. Each bundle that touches a required-reason API
  needs its own copy at its root, and the iOS app, the watch app and the
  complication all compile SharedContainer, so all three get this one.

  What is declared, and why:

  - UserDefaults. CA92.1 is the app's own defaults: the reminder frequency,
    and the pre-2024 break data that CodingFunctions migrates out of on first
    launch. 1C8F.1 is UserDefaults(suiteName:) on the App Group, which is how
    the watch app hands the complication its snapshot. The complication only
    needs the second of those; it carries both because this is one shared
    file and declaring a reason you do not exercise costs nothing.

  - Other data, not linked to the user. A presence document goes to Firestore
    for the five minutes of a break and then deletes itself: a name rolled
    from the curated pool, an optional country, a timezone offset, two
    timestamps. It is deliberately unlinkable - ownerHash is
    sha256(uid + breakId), so two breaks by the same person cannot be
    connected to each other, and no uid is ever written down. None of it is
    used for tracking.

  Checked and deliberately absent: nothing in the project reads a file
  timestamp, the system boot time, available disk space or the active
  keyboard, and the country comes from Locale rather than from location
  services, so none of those categories applies.

  This file is not the App Store Connect privacy questionnaire. That is
  filled in by hand, and the anonymous Firebase account is the item there
  that wants a decision.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
